Composition SHALL preserve workflow autonomy.

7. Composition Components

Every composition SHALL define:

Component	Description
Composition ID	Globally unique identifier
Parent Workflow	Composite workflow
Child Workflows	Reused workflow definitions
Composition Interfaces	Interaction contracts
Dependencies	Execution dependencies
Governance Scope	Applicable governance
8. Composition Patterns

Atlas defines the following canonical composition patterns.

Pattern	Description
Sequential	Ordered workflow execution
Parallel	Concurrent execution
Hierarchical	Parent-child workflow structure
Conditional	Context-dependent composition
Event-Driven	Triggered by events
Pipeline	Output of one becomes input of another
Composite	Nested reusable workflow modules

Additional patterns MAY be introduced through governed extensions.

9. Workflow Interfaces

Every reusable Workflow Definition SHALL define an explicit interface.

Interfaces SHALL specify:

Accepted inputs
Produced outputs
Entry conditions
Exit conditions
Generated events
Error conditions
Supported versions

Interfaces SHALL remain versioned.

10. Dependency Management

Workflow compositions SHALL explicitly declare:

Execution dependencies
Data dependencies
Resource dependencies
Policy dependencies
Timing dependencies
External dependencies

Circular dependencies SHOULD be rejected unless explicitly supported by a governed orchestration profile.

11. Hierarchical Composition

Workflow Definitions MAY contain nested Workflow Definitions.

Example:

Building Construction
│
├── Site Preparation
├── Foundation
├── Structure
│      ├── Columns
│      ├── Beams
│      └── Slabs
├── MEP Installation
└── Inspection

Each child workflow SHALL remain independently versioned.

12. Composition Validation

Every composed workflow SHALL be validated for:

Interface compatibility
Dependency consistency
State compatibility
Policy compatibility
Version compatibility
Resource conflicts
Event consistency

Validation SHALL precede publication.

13. Composition Lifecycle

Every composed workflow SHALL support:

Designed
     │
Validated
     │
Approved
     │
Published
     │
Executed
     │
Maintained
     │
Retired

Lifecycle SHALL remain independently traceable.

14. Governance

Every workflow composition SHALL define:

Composition owner
Workflow owners
Approval authority
Applicable policies
Governance domain
Audit requirements

Governance SHALL remain attached throughout the composition lifecycle.

15. Quality Requirements

Every workflow composition SHALL satisfy:

Modularity
Correctness
Determinism
Explainability
Reusability
Traceability
Auditability
Governance compliance

Quality SHALL be continuously evaluated.

16. Conformance

A Workflow Composition implementation conforms if it:

Supports canonical composition patterns.
Preserves workflow identities.
Defines explicit interfaces.
Validates dependencies.
Supports hierarchical composition.
Maintains governance metadata.
Preserves traceability.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted workflow composition.
Semantic workflow discovery.
Dynamic workflow assembly.
Adaptive composition strategies.
Cross-federation workflow libraries.
Domain-specific composition profiles.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical composition semantics.

